  "findings": [
    {
      "description": "Irreversible production migration: hardcoded DROP COLUMN statements execute directly against the production PostgreSQL endpoint without dry-run, backup, or rollback plan. Any failure or wrong assumption causes permanent data loss.",
      "category": "data-loss",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "description": "Hardcoded production database connection string (postgres://prod-cluster.internal:5432/app) is embedded in source code, exposing internal infrastructure details and making environment-specific configuration impossible.",
      "category": "secret",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "description": "cleanup_files() unconditionally removes the entire BACKUP_DIR tree with shutil.rmtree(ignore_errors=True). If BACKUP_DIR is unset, empty, or misconfigured, it can delete backups or unrelated files without recovery.",
      "category": "data-loss",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "description": "No safety guard or confirmation gate exists for any destructive operation; the migration and cleanup are designed to be irreversible by default.",
      "category": "logic-bug",
      "severity": "high"
    }
  ],
  "decision": "HOLD",
  "fix_description": "All four findings involve irreversible, high-risk production changes (L2). Proposed fix plan (requires human approval before execution): (1) remove the hardcoded production connection string and read it from environment variables/secrets manager; (2) replace direct DROP COLUMN execution with a reversible migration path: require explicit confirmation flag, use a transaction with dry-run verification, create/retain backups, and run only against a staging or migration-approved endpoint; (3) guard cleanup_files() so BACKUP_DIR must be explicitly set and validated as a known backup directory, never delete a root/empty/unset path, and only delete files matching a explicit allowlist; (4) add confirmation gates and fail-closed checks for all destructive operations. Since these are production data-loss/security-sensitive changes, mark needs-approval; do not auto-apply until human approval is granted.",
